@startuml devops
title Build / DevOps / Deploy View\nFrom developer push through quality gates to Azure Container Apps
caption Same PowerShell build runs locally (privatebuild) and in CI. Octopus owns both app deploy and DB migrations.

skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #566573
  BackgroundColor<<dev>> #FDF3E7
  BackgroundColor<<ci>> #E8EEF7
  BackgroundColor<<deploy>> #F0E8F7
  BackgroundColor<<run>> #E8F4E8
}

rectangle "Developer" <<dev>> as dev
rectangle "Git repo\n(GitHub)" <<dev>> as git
rectangle "PrivateBuild.ps1\nbuild.ps1 / BuildFunctions.ps1" <<ci>> as build
rectangle "Quality gates\n- dotnet build (Release)\n- UnitTests 273\n- DbUp migrate\n- IntegrationTests 119" <<ci>> as gates
rectangle "AcceptanceTests\n(Playwright, 88)" <<ci>> as accept
rectangle "Docker image\n(Dockerfile)" <<deploy>> as docker
rectangle "Octopus Deploy\n(.octopus)" <<deploy>> as octo
cloud "Azure Container Apps" <<run>> as aca
database "SQL Server\n(DbUp scripts)" <<run>> as sql

dev --> git : push / PR
git --> build : CI trigger
build --> gates : compile + test
gates --> accept : before PR
build --> docker : package
docker --> octo
accept --> octo : gate passed
octo --> aca : deploy
octo --> sql : run migrations
aca --> sql : runtime

note bottom of build
  Build/DevOps code ~800 LOC PowerShell.
  Do NOT modify .octopus / build scripts
  without approval (repo rule).
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Stage |
|<#FDF3E7> | Source control |
|<#E8EEF7> | Build + quality gates |
|<#F0E8F7> | Packaging + deployment |
|<#E8F4E8> | Runtime environment |
endlegend
@enduml
